  "question": {
    "text": "Let the lines <math><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>30</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> make equal intercepts of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn></math> units with a circle <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>C</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> whose centre lies on <math><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>, then the equation of the circle <math><mi>C</mi></math> is"
